---
import ToolLayout from '@/layouts/ToolLayout.astro'
import YamlToJson from '@/components/tools/data/YamlToJson.tsx'
---

<ToolLayout slug="yaml-to-json">
  <YamlToJson client:load />

  <Fragment slot="explainer">
    <h2>How to convert YAML to JSON</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Paste the YAML or drop a <code>.yaml</code> / <code>.yml</code> file onto the left pane.</li>
      <li>Read any error. The tool reports problems with the exact line and column, and shows the line with a caret under the error.</li>
      <li>Pick the boolean rules. Leave the toggle off for YAML 1.2 behaviour, or turn it on if your file uses <code>yes</code> and <code>no</code> for true and false.</li>
      <li>Choose how to handle multiple documents. A stream separated by <code>---</code> can become a JSON array or only its first document.</li>
      <li>Copy or download the JSON, minified or pretty printed.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>What the YAML parser understands</h2>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full min-w-max border-collapse text-sm">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th class="border-b px-3 py-2 text-left font-semibold">YAML feature</th>
            <th class="border-b px-3 py-2 text-left font-semibold">Supported</th>
            <th class="border-b px-3 py-2 text-left font-semibold">Notes</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="border-b px-3 py-2">Block mappings and sequences</td>
            <td class="border-b px-3 py-2">Yes</td>
            <td class="border-b px-3 py-2">Any nesting depth, including maps that start on a <code>-</code> line</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="border-b px-3 py-2">Flow collections</td>
            <td class="border-b px-3 py-2">Yes</td>
            <td class="border-b px-3 py-2"><code>[a, b]</code> and <code>&#123;k: v&#125;</code>, including across several lines</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="border-b px-3 py-2">Block scalars</td>
            <td class="border-b px-3 py-2">Yes</td>
            <td class="border-b px-3 py-2"><code>|</code>, <code>&gt;</code> with <code>+</code>/<code>-</code> chomping and indentation digits</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="border-b px-3 py-2">Quoted scalars</td>
            <td class="border-b px-3 py-2">Yes</td>
            <td class="border-b px-3 py-2">Single quotes with <code>''</code>, double quotes with <code>\n</code>, <code>\t</code>, <code>\uNNNN</code></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="border-b px-3 py-2">Comments</td>
            <td class="border-b px-3 py-2">Yes</td>
            <td class="border-b px-3 py-2">Recognised and skipped, also at end of line; JSON cannot keep them</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="border-b px-3 py-2">Multi-document streams</td>
            <td class="border-b px-3 py-2">Yes</td>
            <td class="border-b px-3 py-2"><code>---</code> and <code>...</code> boundaries</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="border-b px-3 py-2">Anchors, aliases, merge keys</td>
            <td class="border-b px-3 py-2">No</td>
            <td class="border-b px-3 py-2">Reported as an error, not dropped without notice</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="border-b px-3 py-2">Custom tags, explicit <code>? key</code></td>
            <td class="border-b px-3 py-2">No</td>
            <td class="border-b px-3 py-2">Rare outside hand-written YAML; also reported as an error</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>Three common YAML mistakes</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Tabs: YAML does not allow tabs in indentation. Editors that expand tabs to spaces hide the problem until
        a build fails; here you get “Tabs cannot be used for indentation” with the exact line.
      </li>
      <li>
        An unquoted value that contains “: ”: <code>title: Report: Q3</code> is not a string. The parser reads a
        nested mapping and gives an error. Quote the value.
      </li>
      <li>
        Inconsistent indentation: sibling keys must start in the same column. One extra space gives “this line is
        indented 3 spaces but the mapping around it uses 2”.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Type resolution</h2>
    <p>
      Plain scalars are resolved with the YAML 1.2 core schema: <code>null</code> and <code>~</code> become
      null; <code>true</code>/<code>false</code> become booleans; decimal, hexadecimal (<code>0x1f</code>),
      octal (<code>0o17</code>) and binary (<code>0b1011</code>) integers become numbers, as do floats and
      exponents. Underscores used as digit separators are removed. All other values stay strings, including
      dates, because JSON has no date type.
    </p>
    <p>
      Two YAML values have no JSON equivalent: <code>.inf</code> and <code>.nan</code>. The tool writes them as
      <code>null</code> and shows a notice, so the output is always valid JSON.
    </p>

    <h2>Runs in your browser</h2>
    <p>
      The YAML parser is written for this page and bundled with it, so there is no library download or API
      call. Kubernetes manifests, CI pipelines and Ansible inventories often name internal hosts and services,
      and they stay on your computer.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
</ToolLayout>
